OL,3,GUK long range forecast                 
OL,5,COutlook for Thu 26 Nov to Sat 5 DecFThe
OL,6,FUK is likely to remain in some degree  
OL,7,Fof 'battleground' scenario through     
OL,8,Fmuch of this period, as Atlantic       
OL,9,Fweather systems butt up against high   
OL,10,Fpressure to the east or northeast of   
OL,11,Fthe UK. As such, western and           
OL,12,Fsouthwestern areas are most likely to  
OL,13,Fbe wettest, whereas drier conditions   
OL,14,Fare more probable towards the north    
OL,15,Fand east. That said, some              
OL,16,Fprecipitation is possible for all      
OL,17,Fparts at times. There remains the      
OL,18,Fpotential for snow, especially across  
OL,19,Fthe higher ground of northern UK. In   
OL,20,Fthe north, temperatures overall could  
OL,21,Fbe below normal during this period and 
OL,22,Fperhaps closer to normal in the south, 
OL,23,Fand the boundary between milder/coldere
OL,24,Fconditions will be determined by how TV
